  "source_url": "https://nextgenforearth.org/",
  "captured_at": "2026-11-25T14:42:16.650974+00:00",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Training Africa's Next Generation of Climate Scientists",
      "body": "NextGen for Earth builds research capacity, climate literacy, and community resilience across Africa — through rigorous training, peer mentorship, and published science.\n\n\"Youth don't just inherit the climate crisis — they are its most powerful solution.\""
    },
    {
      "heading": "Empowering Youth to Lead Bold Climate Action",
      "body": "We want to empower youth to take the lead in climate research, policy, and community action. We want to build a global community where young people connect across borders, share knowledge, and drive solutions grounded in sustainability, equity, and the circular economy.\n\nWe work with communities, educators, civil society, and decision-makers to make sure youth voices don't just speak — they shape the future of climate action."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Building a Global Climate Community",
      "body": "A global community where young people connect across borders, share knowledge, and drive solutions grounded in sustainability, equity, and the circular economy — making sure youth voices shape the future of climate action."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Youth-Led Innovation for a Regenerative World",
      "body": "We want youth to lead bold, inclusive climate action — from local initiatives to global platforms. Communities generating their own evidence, shifting behaviours, and co-creating sustainable solutions that reflect their realities."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Science × Community × Action",
      "body": "We believe youth-led innovation and intergenerational collaboration can build a regenerative world — where everyone shares the power and responsibility to protect our planet."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Four Programmes. One Mission.",
      "body": ""
    },
    {
      "heading": "Research Capacity Building",
      "body": "Weekly training for early career researchers in methods, systematic reviews, grant writing, data synthesis, and ethics."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Healthcare Worker Training",
      "body": "Monthly training equipping frontline health workers to understand and respond to climate-driven health challenges."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Youth Climate Stewardship",
      "body": "School students mentored by trained youth peers on climate literacy, tree planting, and environmental action."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Indigenous Knowledge Transfer",
      "body": "Preserving and amplifying traditional ecological wisdom as a cornerstone of climate adaptation and resilience."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Our Training Programmes",
      "body": "Three distinct training tracks delivered through regular workshops — each designed to build lasting capacity where it matters most.\n\nResearch Methods & Study Design\n\nSystematic Reviews\n\nData Collection & Management\n\nSynthesising Evidence\n\nGrant Writing\n\nResearch Ethics & Safeguarding\n\nClimate Change & Health Fundamentals\n\nHeat Impacts on Patient Care\n\nExtreme Weather & Service Delivery\n\nClimate Disrespectful Care\n\nCommunity Resilience Strategies\n\nMental Health & Climate Stress\n\nClimate Science Fundamentals\n\nEnvironmental Stewardship\n\nTree Planting & Restoration\n\nPeer-to-Peer Mentorship\n\nCommunity Engagement\n\nMental Health Peer Support"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Theory of Change",
      "body": "How we move from training and science to lasting climate impact across Africa.\n\nExpert mentors\n\nPublished science\n\nCommunity partnerships\n\nFunded programmes\n\nWeekly workshops\n\nPeer mentorship\n\nField research\n\nTree planting drives\n\n100+ youth trained\n\n35 researchers mentored\n\n4,000+ children reached\n\n12 publications\n\nYouth lead research\n\nSchools adopt stewardship\n\nCommunities more resilient\n\nPolicies informed\n\nClimate-literate generation\n\nEvidence-based policy\n\nHealthier communities\n\nSustainable Africa"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Our Research & Publications",
      "body": "From heat impacts on pregnant women in Kilifi to youth-inclusive climate strategies across sub-Saharan Africa — our research shapes policy, informs communities, and drives meaningful change. All work is peer-reviewed and freely accessible."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Aware but unprepared: climate change impacts on healthcare workers in Africa — a scoping review",
      "body": "Lusambili A et al.\n\nFrontiers in Public Health · 13, 1693703"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Towards youth-inclusive strategies for climate change and health research in sub-Saharan Africa",
      "body": "Lusambili AM et al.\n\nJournal of Climate Change and Health · 22, 100418"
    },
