    },
    {
      "heading": "Community co-design workshop on reducing heat exposure impacts on pregnant women in Kilifi, Kenya",
      "body": "Lusambili A et al.\n\nFrontiers in Public Health · 11, 1146048"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Awareness and interventions to reduce dehydration in pregnant women and newborns in rural Kenya",
      "body": "Lusambili A, Nakstad B\n\nAfrican Journal of Primary Health Care & Family Medicine · 15(1), e1-e3"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Mapping the Impact of Climate Seasonality on Ageing",
      "body": "How does the changing climate shape the everyday lives of older Africans? This study finds out — and listens to those most at risk.\n\nThis study examines how climate seasonality shapes the lived experiences of ageing in Busia and Kilifi counties, Kenya . We identify who is most affected, assess how seasonal climate variability influences health and wellbeing, and analyse the resilience and adaptation strategies at individual, household, and community levels."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Fund the Next Generation",
      "body": "Your investment directly trains young African scientists, equips healthcare workers, and puts climate knowledge into the hands of school children."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Youth Research Fellowship",
      "body": "Fund one early career researcher through a full year of mentorship, training, and their first peer-reviewed publication."
    },
    {
      "heading": "School Climate Stewardship",
      "body": "Sponsor weekly climate workshops and tree-planting drives across a cluster of schools in Kenya or Ethiopia."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Healthcare Worker Training",
      "body": "Train a cohort of healthcare workers on climate-health impacts, equipping frontline staff to protect vulnerable communities."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Global Youth Science Network",
      "body": "Connect our youth ambassadors with young scientists across the globe — funding travel, networking events, and international collaborations.\n\nWant to discuss a bespoke partnership? We welcome conversations with foundations, trusts, and institutional donors. Contact us at team@nextgenforearth.org or Comms@nextgenforearth.org"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Research & Institutional Partners",
      "body": "We collaborate with leading universities, health departments, ministries, and civil society organisations across Africa and internationally."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Gallery",
      "body": "Moments from our research, community engagement, and youth leadership work across Africa."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Our Work In Action",
      "body": "See the science. Meet the people. Feel the impact.\n\nWatch NextGen for Earth in action — from field research to community engagement and youth leadership across Africa."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Led by Scientists. Driven by Youth.",
      "body": "Our team spans four continents — combining senior research expertise with frontline youth energy to create change that is both rigorous and deeply rooted."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Regional Ambassadors Across the Continent",
      "body": ""
    },
    {
      "heading": "What Our Community Says",
      "body": "NextGen for Earth showed me that youth are not just the future of climate action — we are the present. I now engage directly with policymakers on environmental stewardship.\n\nNextGen for Earth gave me the skills to conduct and publish a scoping review. I went from a student with no research experience to a peer-reviewed author — in one year."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Ready to Invest in Africa's Climate Future? Your funding trains researchers, empowers communities, and plants the seeds of lasting change.",
      "body": ""
    },
    {
      "heading": "We'd Love to Hear From You",
      "body": "Whether you are a donor, researcher, partner organisation, or young person wanting to join — we welcome every conversation.\n\nMokoyeti West Road, off Langata Road, Karen, Nairobi, Kenya (+254) 735 920 920\n\nSubscribe to our newsletter for research breakthroughs, training updates, and programme launches.\n\nTo subscribe write to Comms@nextgenforearth.org\n\nA pan-African network training young climate scientists, empowering healthcare workers, and building resilient communities across Africa.\n\nHome\n\nAbout\n\nTraining\n\nResearch\n\nFund Our Work\n\nOur Team\n\nEarly Career Researchers\n\nHealthcare Workers\n\nYouth Climate Stewards\n\nIndigenous Knowledge\n\n© 2025 NextGen for Earth. All rights reserved.\n\nPrivacy Policy\n\nOur Policies\n\nPublications"
    }
